  "post": {
    "title": "The Moon visits Jupiter and Mars on Monday 🌔 Sky This Week, Nov 30–Dec 6",
    "description": "Before dawn on Mon 30 Nov, look high in the south-east: the Moon, Jupiter and Mars make a tight group. The Moon's closest pass to Jupiter (1.9°) happens in daylight that morning, and to Mars (3.7°) that evening. All week before sunrise, Venus (magnitude -4.8) shines low in the south-east, 23° up around 06:40 mid-week.\n\nPositions computed for central Europe (50°N, 15°E) with astronomy-engine. Narration uses a synthetic voice.",
